WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.810
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:11.080 --> 00:13.331
Do you think...

3
00:13.332 --> 00:18.629
Carabaos have dreams when they sleep?

4
00:20.381 --> 00:21.883
Of course.

5
00:22.633 --> 00:25.720
What do you think they dream of?

6
00:27.889 --> 00:31.476
The sweetest grass they can eat.

7
00:32.393 --> 00:34.687
Why do you ask?

8
00:36.439 --> 00:39.400
It looks like he's sleeping soundly.

9
00:42.862 --> 00:44.697
Bong.

10
00:45.865 --> 00:47.658
I have a question.

11
00:49.869 --> 00:51.870
What is it?

12
00:51.871 --> 00:53.914
But...

13
00:53.915 --> 00:56.876
Promise me you won't laugh.

14
00:59.796 --> 01:03.674
Now that you say it, of course I am gonna laugh.

15
01:05.426 --> 01:08.387
I was just wondering.

16
01:11.724 --> 01:15.560
Gone is the day before you can finish the question.

17
01:15.561 --> 01:17.271
Wait.

18
01:18.731 --> 01:21.109
I just want to know...

19
01:23.069 --> 01:25.780
if one of us...

20
01:27.198 --> 01:30.075
leaves the world first.

21
01:30.076 --> 01:32.536
What if I die?

22
01:32.537 --> 01:39.544
- Will you look for me? - Yes.

23
01:52.557 --> 01:55.767
Our families expect us

24
01:55.768 --> 02:02.191
to marry someone and raise a family.

25
02:04.652 --> 02:07.529
But first...

26
02:07.530 --> 02:13.451
our families expect us

27
02:13.452 --> 02:17.915
to make money.

28
02:19.500 --> 02:22.086
That is true.

29
02:23.796 --> 02:26.549
They expect a lot.

30
02:27.758 --> 02:32.179
Sometimes, I wish...

31
02:32.180 --> 02:35.099
I wish it could always be like this.

32
02:38.519 --> 02:42.064
Like what?

33
02:44.734 --> 02:48.279
You and me, together.

34
02:54.535 --> 02:59.624
I think the carabao is getting jealous.

35
02:59.700 --> 03:05.500
"All the Things I Leave You" (Episode 4)

36
03:42.124 --> 03:44.167
If he's the one to make my heart weak...

37
03:44.168 --> 03:46.629
Oh, I’d love it.

38
03:47.755 --> 03:50.465
And you have the guts to say.

39
03:50.466 --> 03:53.468
"The first one to fall, loses."

40
03:53.469 --> 03:54.469
Whatever.

41
03:54.470 --> 03:55.720
Look, Jorge.

42
03:55.721 --> 03:56.805
Handsome. Check.

43
03:56.806 --> 03:58.932
Smells good. Check.

44
03:58.933 --> 04:01.184
Knows how to dress. Check.

45
04:01.185 --> 04:03.645
Has a big...

46
04:03.646 --> 04:04.272
Ruth.

47
04:04.273 --> 04:05.897
- What? - Stop it.

48
04:05.898 --> 04:08.650
I meant wallet.

49
04:08.651 --> 04:10.653
He has a big wallet.

50
04:12.488 --> 04:15.282
I said, he has a big wallet.

51
04:15.283 --> 04:19.078
You're thinking of something else.

52
04:20.955 --> 04:24.292
Oh, here's the other one.

53
04:32.425 --> 04:34.676
I brought something to cook.

54
04:34.677 --> 04:38.388
Isn't miki Grandpa Tino's favorite?

55
04:38.389 --> 04:39.764
How sweet.

56
04:39.765 --> 04:42.434
I wish he wasn't a cheater.

57
04:42.435 --> 04:43.768
- Ruth. - Huh?

58
04:43.769 --> 04:44.894
Nothing!

59
04:44.895 --> 04:47.731
I said, sweet.

60
04:47.732 --> 04:50.610
I wish it was sweeter.

61
05:00.911 --> 05:01.787
Yeah.

62
05:01.787 --> 05:02.787
Wait.

63
05:04.957 --> 05:06.375
Miss me?

64
05:11.130 --> 05:13.340
Stupid.

65
05:13.341 --> 05:15.425
You disappeared.

66
05:15.426 --> 05:17.970
You disappeared too.

67
05:18.971 --> 05:20.722
I'm sorry.

68
05:20.723 --> 05:24.643
I had to do something.

69
05:25.770 --> 05:28.189
Is it Agnes?

70
05:29.690 --> 05:32.068
We're not together.

71
05:34.362 --> 05:38.074
Why are you lying about it?

72
05:38.908 --> 05:40.826
It's so obvious.

73
05:42.286 --> 05:44.079
We used to date.

74
05:44.080 --> 05:45.872
But...

75
05:45.873 --> 05:48.041
We're over now.

76
05:48.042 --> 05:50.419
Why don't you believe me?

77
05:51.087 --> 05:52.420
Why?

78
05:52.421 --> 05:54.173
You jealous?

79
05:55.675 --> 05:58.302
Why would I be jealous?

80
05:59.470 --> 06:01.596
You're clearly jealous.

81
06:01.597 --> 06:02.848
I’m not.

82
06:03.057 --> 06:04.600
Jorge?

83
06:05.434 --> 06:09.938
Your Grandpa Tino has a box of jewelry in his room.

84
06:09.939 --> 06:11.899
Can you look for it?

85
06:12.108 --> 06:13.650
Now, Auntie?

86
06:13.651 --> 06:14.776
Yes, please.

87
06:14.777 --> 06:18.030
But don't tell Lilia, okay?

88
06:26.205 --> 06:27.956
I'll just look for it.

89
06:27.957 --> 06:31.418
Do you want to come to the room with me?

90
06:31.419 --> 06:32.836
Hey!

91
06:32.837 --> 06:35.797
What will you do in the room again?

92
06:35.798 --> 06:38.216
Ruth, we'll look for...

93
06:38.217 --> 06:39.801
Kiko, come with me.

94
06:39.802 --> 06:40.803
Come on.

95
06:41.303 --> 06:42.345
To where?

96
06:42.346 --> 06:43.555
The kitchen.

97
06:43.556 --> 06:44.597
I have something to ask.

98
06:44.598 --> 06:47.725
What kind of miki do you want to cook?

99
06:47.726 --> 06:48.561
I’ll come too.

100
06:48.562 --> 06:52.481
No, you make coffee and serve them.

101
06:53.899 --> 06:57.193
What other kind of miki is there?

102
06:57.194 --> 06:58.821
Just follow me.

103
07:02.324 --> 07:03.117
What is it, Ruth?

104
07:03.118 --> 07:05.160
I have something to ask.

105
07:05.161 --> 07:06.286
Any kind works.

106
07:06.287 --> 07:07.662
It's not that.

107
07:07.663 --> 07:09.539
Do you like my cousin?

108
07:09.540 --> 07:10.540
Huh?

109
07:11.083 --> 07:13.669
I don't like liars.

110
07:15.963 --> 07:17.464
If I said yes,

111
07:17.465 --> 07:18.965
what will you do?

112
07:18.966 --> 07:20.216
Ha!

113
07:20.217 --> 07:22.261
For real?

114
07:24.722 --> 07:27.140
Wow, lobster.

115
07:27.141 --> 07:32.188
Oh, yeah. Someone wanted miki with lobster.

116
07:33.147 --> 07:37.151
The mayor’s son brought it... Nathan.

117
07:38.402 --> 07:39.361
For real?

118
07:39.362 --> 07:41.030
He's rich.

119
07:48.787 --> 07:50.538
Don't worry.

120
07:50.539 --> 07:53.166
Let's make your miki more delicious.

121
07:53.167 --> 07:55.835
Does it mean...

122
07:55.836 --> 07:57.755
You like me more?

123
07:58.923 --> 08:01.425
We'll see.

124
08:01.884 --> 08:03.719
Okay, let’s see.

125
08:04.053 --> 08:05.638
Insiong.

126
08:07.348 --> 08:08.307
Lilia.

127
08:08.308 --> 08:09.766
Look at your son.

128
08:09.767 --> 08:12.895
He and Kiko might be doing something.

129
08:13.729 --> 08:18.359
It might also be a reason why he doesn't want to study in Manila.

130
08:19.360 --> 08:20.903
You may be wrong.

131
08:21.987 --> 08:27.742
Jorge probably believes

132
08:27.743 --> 08:31.497
that he will manage the restaurant.

133
08:35.084 --> 08:36.960
You're drunk, Insiong.

134
08:36.961 --> 08:39.004
Stop it.

135
08:40.339 --> 08:44.510
Keep in mind, Dad isn't here anymore to solve your problems.

136
08:45.594 --> 08:47.845
And my god, this Jorge.

137
08:47.846 --> 08:51.308
I hope he makes the right choice for his future.

138
08:53.060 --> 08:54.228
Lilia.

139
08:55.896 --> 08:57.773
What more do you want?

140
08:59.692 --> 09:00.859
Insiong.

141
09:03.279 --> 09:05.739
Hello, Mayor!

142
09:17.751 --> 09:21.630
- Having a good drink, are we? - Good evening, Mayor.

143
09:22.881 --> 09:26.384
Thank you for visiting us.

144
09:26.385 --> 09:29.847
It's forbidden to say thanks at a wake.

145
09:30.723 --> 09:34.517
Oh no, the elders have so many beliefs

146
09:34.518 --> 09:41.275
that I don't even remember it's bad to say thanks at a wake.

147
09:42.610 --> 09:47.322
It would be wrong not to visit on the last night of the wake.

148
09:47.323 --> 09:51.826
We all know how much the migrant farmers have helped our town.

149
09:51.827 --> 09:54.662
Yes, mayor. Thank you.

150
09:54.663 --> 09:55.956
Auntie.

151
09:58.500 --> 10:02.712
Is this really Nathan? You look so handsome.

152
10:02.713 --> 10:06.549
I should've been the one to welcome you.

153
10:06.550 --> 10:09.802
You look so much like your father.

154
10:09.803 --> 10:11.095
Mayor, wait for a bit.

155
10:11.096 --> 10:13.557
Jorge!

156
10:14.183 --> 10:15.308
Jorge!

157
10:15.309 --> 10:16.476
This is urgent!

158
10:16.477 --> 10:18.728
Nathan's here!

159
10:18.729 --> 10:20.271
Oh, Nathan. This is Jorge.

160
10:20.272 --> 10:23.441
Jorge, this is Nathan.

161
10:23.442 --> 10:25.485
- Oh yeah, Auntie. - Remember?

162
10:25.486 --> 10:28.780
We met back at the gate earlier. He was waving at me.

163
10:28.781 --> 10:31.492
But I think he forgot who I am.

164
10:32.845 --> 10:34.179
How can I forget you?

165
10:34.203 --> 10:36.329
Yeah, I waved at you because you were waving at me.

166
10:36.330 --> 10:37.455
Right?

167
10:37.456 --> 10:37.956
See?

168
10:37.957 --> 10:39.707
You already forgot.

169
10:39.708 --> 10:41.042
Don't you remember?

170
10:41.043 --> 10:43.295
When we were in kindergarten?

171
10:48.550 --> 10:50.802
Nat-Nat the Fat?

172
10:50.803 --> 10:53.638
See? Even up to now, you're still a bully.

173
10:53.639 --> 10:55.640
So it’s you.

174
10:55.641 --> 10:56.641
I didn't mean it.

175
10:56.642 --> 10:58.601
I just remembered.

176
10:58.602 --> 11:00.478
I remember only.

177
11:00.479 --> 11:02.730
Do I still deserve to be called that?

178
11:02.731 --> 11:04.274
Nat-Nat the Fat?

179
11:07.820 --> 11:08.779
Okay.

180
11:08.780 --> 11:10.071
I'll let you talk here.

181
11:10.095 --> 11:13.598
I'll leave you and I'm going to help in there, okay?

182
11:16.245 --> 11:17.496
Kiko!

183
11:18.372 --> 11:19.915
Come help me here.

184
11:27.840 --> 11:32.260
Your bodyguards are intense. Watching your every move.

185
11:32.261 --> 11:33.053
Of course.

186
11:33.054 --> 11:36.014
So if you bully me... You already know.

187
11:39.685 --> 11:42.646
That was a long time ago.

188
11:43.856 --> 11:46.400
I'm only kidding, you know.

189
11:47.693 --> 11:49.360
You're not fat anymore.

190
11:49.361 --> 11:51.696
I mean, you're not fat.

191
11:51.697 --> 11:52.406
You're...

192
11:52.406 --> 11:52.906
Uh...

193
11:52.907 --> 11:55.909
You’re... What do you call it?

194
11:56.452 --> 11:58.996
What, handsome?

195
12:01.832 --> 12:03.083
A little bit.

196
12:03.542 --> 12:04.792
Wow!

197
12:04.793 --> 12:07.545
Your standards are so high.

198
12:07.546 --> 12:11.382
Maybe you're like that with the people you like.

199
12:11.383 --> 12:12.383
No.

200
12:14.511 --> 12:16.387
So...

201
12:16.388 --> 12:19.433
Are you single?

202
12:22.728 --> 12:24.605
We should hang out sometime.

203
12:27.232 --> 12:30.944
Like play basketball or something, silly.

204
12:34.531 --> 12:36.700
Do you still know how to speak Ilocano?

205
12:37.576 --> 12:39.285
A little bit.

206
12:39.286 --> 12:40.287
No?

207
12:42.289 --> 12:44.465
Not anymore? Just...

208
12:45.375 --> 12:46.709
Even a little?

209
12:46.710 --> 12:48.212
A little.

210
12:57.638 --> 12:59.096
It's mine now.

211
12:59.097 --> 13:00.808
This one's expensive.

212
13:01.225 --> 13:02.391
- Do you like it? - Expensive?

213
13:02.392 --> 13:03.935
- Yeah. - C'mon.

214
13:03.936 --> 13:05.019
Do you want to try it?

215
13:05.020 --> 13:06.562
Is it mine now?

216
13:06.563 --> 13:07.980
Yeah, you want to try?

217
13:07.981 --> 13:09.899
Of course, no problem.

218
13:09.900 --> 13:11.109
Okay.

219
13:15.864 --> 13:19.742
Wow, that looks nice on you.

220
13:19.743 --> 13:20.743
Nice?

221
13:20.744 --> 13:24.748
Yeah, this looks kinda nice on you.

222
13:25.332 --> 13:29.378
You can't even wear a jacket in the Philippines but I like it.

223
13:33.215 --> 13:35.925
I hope you like...

224
13:35.926 --> 13:37.844
crumbs.

225
13:37.845 --> 13:41.139
Uh, I guess.

226
13:41.890 --> 13:43.975
Nathan, this is Kiko.

227
13:43.976 --> 13:45.477
Kiko, this is Nathan.

228
13:47.187 --> 13:50.356
He's my childhood friend and...

229
13:50.357 --> 13:51.400
We are...

230
13:52.401 --> 13:54.402
Why am I talking to you in English?

231
13:54.403 --> 13:58.281
Didn't Auntie give you something to do?

232
13:58.282 --> 14:00.032
Well?

233
14:00.033 --> 14:02.202
- Oh, right. - You're just gonna stand there?

234
14:04.454 --> 14:08.500
I'll give this to you first and give this back when you come back to the Philippines.

235
14:09.960 --> 14:11.753
Yeah, yeah. It's okay.

236
14:12.296 --> 14:13.671
Do you want some?

237
14:13.672 --> 14:15.841
I think this is mine. I don't know.

238
14:16.216 --> 14:17.925
I'll just get you a new one.

239
14:17.926 --> 14:19.553
Okay.

240
14:46.830 --> 14:50.000
Who's jealous now?

241
14:51.501 --> 14:53.127
Me?

242
14:53.128 --> 14:54.838
Jealous?

243
14:56.506 --> 15:00.260
I know how kids from political clans act.

244
15:01.553 --> 15:05.473
They think they’re descended from gods.

245
15:05.474 --> 15:06.766
Hey.

246
15:06.767 --> 15:09.061
Nathan's a good guy.

247
15:15.943 --> 15:17.443
Hey!

248
15:17.444 --> 15:20.071
Be careful with those.

249
15:20.072 --> 15:22.782
Do you want Grandpa to haunt you?

250
15:22.783 --> 15:24.826
My bad.

251
15:42.094 --> 15:44.972
Grandpa Tino kept this all this time.

252
15:46.056 --> 15:49.350
When I made this for Grandpa Tino...

253
15:49.351 --> 15:52.645
It was the day he told me

254
15:52.646 --> 15:57.275
I'll manage the restaurant someday.

255
16:00.404 --> 16:02.072
Can I see?

256
16:04.241 --> 16:05.951
Look at me.

257
16:10.580 --> 16:13.041
Oh, it's Auntie.

258
16:15.043 --> 16:16.585
Jorge.

259
16:16.586 --> 16:18.671
If you think about it,

260
16:18.672 --> 16:22.801
your grandpa and grandma are together now.

261
16:23.468 --> 16:27.222
Maybe they're going on dates in heaven.

262
16:33.562 --> 16:35.813
Is it true...

263
16:35.814 --> 16:43.814
that the heart remembers even when someone’s long gone?

264
16:45.699 --> 16:47.325
I don't know.

265
16:55.375 --> 16:56.375
Jorge!

266
16:58.128 --> 17:01.757
This is what your aunt is looking for.

267
17:08.388 --> 17:10.390
Isn't it this one?

268
17:11.141 --> 17:12.600
Jorge!

269
17:12.601 --> 17:14.393
Come quick, your dad!

270
17:14.394 --> 17:15.854
Jorge!

271
17:21.735 --> 17:23.987
For my father!

272
17:26.114 --> 17:29.534
Good evening.

273
17:30.994 --> 17:33.454
Friends.

274
17:33.455 --> 17:37.209
And family.

275
17:38.627 --> 17:40.796
Tonight...

276
17:44.549 --> 17:45.716
Tonight,

277
17:45.717 --> 17:48.344
- We will get to know... - Insiong!

278
17:48.345 --> 17:49.888
Stop it.

279
17:51.098 --> 17:53.308
Aren’t you ashamed?

280
17:54.184 --> 17:57.812
- Tonight, we will know... - Insiong!

281
17:57.813 --> 17:59.522
How good...

282
17:59.523 --> 18:01.315
We will know how good my father was.

283
18:01.316 --> 18:04.778
Aren't you ashamed of what you're doing?

284
18:06.405 --> 18:07.656
Anyway.

285
18:13.912 --> 18:16.748
Stop for now.

286
18:18.083 --> 18:21.293
I will tell you...

287
18:21.294 --> 18:23.629
my side of the story.

288
18:23.630 --> 18:25.632
You know...

289
18:30.303 --> 18:33.472
My father

290
18:33.473 --> 18:36.184
loved me so much.

291
18:41.189 --> 18:43.400
Just like how

292
18:45.610 --> 18:47.946
he loved you all.

293
18:48.989 --> 18:51.116
Even Jorge.

294
18:53.410 --> 18:55.745
He loved Jorge

295
18:56.872 --> 18:59.373
far more than he loved me.

296
18:59.374 --> 19:01.710
But you know, Jorge...

297
19:03.378 --> 19:06.463
Your grandpa hated...

298
19:06.464 --> 19:08.967
your mom.

299
19:10.051 --> 19:12.053
Isn't he...

300
19:13.180 --> 19:15.681
Because he thought,

301
19:15.682 --> 19:17.516
your mom was a whore.

302
19:17.517 --> 19:19.060
Dad.

303
19:25.066 --> 19:26.610
Father,

304
19:28.320 --> 19:31.239
did you even love me?

305
19:37.454 --> 19:40.790
You didn't even trust me.

306
19:44.085 --> 19:45.085
You know...

307
19:45.086 --> 19:46.545
Kiko, I can take care of this.

308
19:46.546 --> 19:47.713
- Insiong! - Because...

309
19:47.714 --> 19:51.176
Insiong, stop that. Aren't you ashamed?

310
19:52.260 --> 19:56.263
- Insiong, stop it! - Because he thought so highly of himself!

311
19:56.264 --> 19:59.683
Stop it, Insiong. Have some shame. Sit down.

312
19:59.684 --> 20:00.936
Dad.

313
20:05.148 --> 20:06.441
What?

314
20:06.983 --> 20:08.734
What, Jorge?

315
20:08.735 --> 20:11.238
Is that who you look up to?

316
20:14.824 --> 20:17.827
That's who you want to be like?

317
20:19.621 --> 20:21.331
Him!

318
20:22.457 --> 20:24.458
Insiong!

319
20:24.459 --> 20:26.043
Insiong, stop it.

320
20:26.044 --> 20:27.753
- Stop it, Insiong! - Don’t touch me!

321
20:27.754 --> 20:29.381
Insiong, stop it.

322
20:33.635 --> 20:35.135
Let's go inside.

323
20:35.136 --> 20:36.429
Let's go.

324
20:45.605 --> 20:46.939
No!

325
20:46.940 --> 20:48.400
Insiong.

326
20:49.818 --> 20:53.488
- Stop it. - A lot of people are watching.

327
20:54.698 --> 20:57.659
Insiong. Come on.

328
21:00.829 --> 21:03.330
Stop it.

329
21:03.331 --> 21:04.666
Stop it.

330
21:12.590 --> 21:14.175
Ouchie!

331
21:14.926 --> 21:16.886
You're so dramatic.

332
21:17.345 --> 21:18.722
It hurts.

333
21:23.059 --> 21:24.894
Kiko.

334
21:26.187 --> 21:27.938
I just wondered.

335
21:27.939 --> 21:31.109
When you suggested that I study again...

336
21:36.323 --> 21:38.116
I thought of

337
21:39.492 --> 21:43.204
wanting to be a doctor.

338
21:45.332 --> 21:49.209
Your patient would suffer, doc.

339
21:49.210 --> 21:51.754
Your hands are too heavy.

340
21:51.755 --> 21:54.007
It's why I didn't push through.

341
21:56.176 --> 21:57.761
Jorge.

342
21:58.428 --> 22:00.347
The other day,

343
22:00.972 --> 22:06.561
I had the chance to think about what you said.

344
22:08.188 --> 22:11.274
About the scholarship.

345
22:12.067 --> 22:13.777
What about it?

346
22:14.527 --> 22:15.778
I applied...

347
22:15.779 --> 22:16.780
Kiko!

348
22:17.739 --> 22:23.036
I'm sorry about what Insiong did.

349
22:24.204 --> 22:26.247
Yes, Auntie. It's okay.

350
22:27.290 --> 22:30.085
Have you seen a jewelry box?

351
22:32.462 --> 22:36.256
If you see one, don't tell your Auntie Camilla, okay?

352
22:36.257 --> 22:38.634
Just me.

353
22:38.635 --> 22:40.010
Jorge?

354
22:40.011 --> 22:42.347
Have you seen...

355
22:46.434 --> 22:49.478
I'm so concerned about Kiko.

356
22:49.479 --> 22:51.980
Are you okay now, Kiko?

357
22:51.981 --> 22:53.857
Yes, Auntie. I'm okay.

358
22:53.858 --> 22:57.569
My god, Lilia. I'm so worried for Kiko.

359
22:57.570 --> 22:59.780
It's why I'm here too.

360
22:59.781 --> 23:01.323
Poor kid.

361
23:01.324 --> 23:03.201
But he's okay now.

362
23:10.375 --> 23:13.336
Such a nice boy.

363
23:18.591 --> 23:23.053
It looks like they're competing to be your favorite aunt.

364
23:23.054 --> 23:24.972
They smiled at me.

365
23:24.973 --> 23:26.598
Maybe...

366
23:26.599 --> 23:29.144
They’ll accept me now.

367
23:37.944 --> 23:41.739
This is what they were looking for.

368
23:48.788 --> 23:50.289
But...

369
23:50.290 --> 23:52.417
What's this one?

370
23:56.087 --> 23:58.465
Letters?

371
24:06.598 --> 24:08.683
Do you know him?

372
24:09.559 --> 24:11.143
No.

373
24:11.144 --> 24:15.565
But he looks familiar to me.

374
24:18.526 --> 24:21.738
You look like him. No doubt about it.

375
24:44.177 --> 24:46.845
What's inside that box?

376
24:46.846 --> 24:48.514
Nothing, Auntie.

377
24:48.515 --> 24:50.057
Just pictures.

378
24:50.058 --> 24:52.018
Can I see?

379
24:53.811 --> 24:58.274
Who's Primitivo Pascual?

380
24:59.359 --> 25:00.567
Camilla!

381
25:00.568 --> 25:03.070
Yes, coming!

382
25:03.071 --> 25:06.615
Jorge, don’t forget the jewelry box.

383
25:06.616 --> 25:08.076
Yes, Auntie.

384
25:15.041 --> 25:17.626
Kiko.

385
25:17.627 --> 25:21.421
We can't read these here.

386
25:21.422 --> 25:23.758
Hide them for now?

387
25:26.553 --> 25:28.304
Let's meet tomorrow.

388
25:32.934 --> 25:35.144
Arrange them.

389
25:37.355 --> 25:39.648
You look like him.

390
25:39.649 --> 25:41.317
Let me see.

391
25:45.154 --> 25:47.949
You really look like him.

392
25:51.744 --> 25:53.663
Jorge.

393
25:58.960 --> 26:02.422
My grandpa's name is Bong.

394
26:10.555 --> 26:13.390
“My world,”

395
26:13.391 --> 26:14.392
“Bong.”
